# omp 17.3.7 `--mode rpc` STARTUP frames (agent -> host), in wire order.
#
# Provenance: the credential-free probe harness in omp-rpc-probe-harness.tar.gz spawned
# `omp --mode rpc --model stub-model` (driver3.js:3) with PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR on the child env
# and the workspace as cwd (driver3.js:6-7), driving a local OpenAI-compatible stub model — no
# vendor credential was involved. Every line below is VERBATIM from the named capture unless it
# is marked RECONSTRUCTED, in which case the capture truncated it and the load-bearing fields
# are kept while the elided bulk is dropped.
#
# <- q3-probe3-hosttool-roundtrip.txt:3 (byte-identical at q3-probe2-stub-handshake.txt:7 and
#    q3-probe4-approval-gate.txt:3). `ready` is the FIRST frame and is unconditional
#    (rpc-mode.ts:690): it is the ONLY readiness signal on this plane. protocolVersion 1 is in
#    force until the host negotiates; 2 is offered in supportedProtocolVersions.
{"type":"ready","protocolVersion":1,"supportedProtocolVersions":[1,2],"maxFrameBytes":1048576,"maxReassembledFrameBytes":67108864}
# <- q3-probe3-hosttool-roundtrip.txt:7. FIRE AND FORGET: the setWidget dialog is never awaited
#    (rpc-mode.ts:824), and the probe measured BLOCKING_UI_REQUESTS 0 across the whole run with
#    two of these on the stream. It must never gate a turn.
{"type":"extension_ui_request","id":"155cddcf6a81ec55","method":"setWidget","widgetKey":"autoresearch"}
# <- q3-probe3-hosttool-roundtrip.txt:8, RECONSTRUCTED: the capture truncated ~12 KB of command
#    descriptors ("…(+11905B)"). The first two commands of the captured payload are kept so the
#    line is valid JSON; the adapter reads the frame TYPE, not the catalogue.
{"type":"available_commands_update","commands":[{"name":"security","description":"Plan, run, inspect, import, and compare OMP-native security scans","source":"builtin"},{"name":"model","aliases":["models"],"description":"Show current model selection","source":"builtin"}]}
# <- q3-probe3-hosttool-roundtrip.txt:9. The response to the host's negotiate_protocol,
#    correlated on the host-chosen id "1". Protocol 2 is in force from this frame on.
{"id":"1","type":"response","command":"negotiate_protocol","success":true,"data":{"protocolVersion":2}}
